  "implementation_notes": [
    "Only advertised listChanged capabilities enable persistent caches; unadvertised catalogs are freshly listed. Notifications only invalidate their connection and catalog kind, with resource notifications also invalidating templates.",
    "Refresh serializes fetching and retries one intervening notification; each refresh is bounded by 30 seconds, 100 pages, 2048 items and 64KiB cursor limits, and cyclic/churning catalogs fail without publishing partial pages.",
    "Live runtime discovery, MCP status and inspection consume the connection-owned cache. Catalog snapshots freeze complete definitions; changed/replaced connections reject old tool bindings without closing the healthy current connection. Already-admitted calls may finish.",
    "Existing configured direct-call and permission policies remain unchanged; snapshot admission does not impose a new directory-membership permission. Shutdown/error closes catalog publication along with the owned peer.",
    "Frozen Codex tool catalog uses notification revisions. Its resource/prompt handler only logs notifications; this numbered task explicitly requires resource/prompt cache invalidation, implemented at the existing inspection boundary. Resource subscription remains reported as unsupported."
  ],
